    "created_at": "2021-11-04T10:15:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-11-04T10:15:43Z",
    "body": "> Actually, I'm not sure. Doing a cache lookup synchronously seems bad, but perhaps that is what implementations do? That probably warrants a bit more investigation. One way to do it later in \"main fetch\" would be to check the value of _recursive_ I suppose, although that might still run into problems with HTTP authentication requests.\n\nCache lookup *should* be synchronous IMO as it relies on something controlled by the main thread, making it parallel would create either locks or unnecessary races.\n\nMaybe keeping it where I put it is correct?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
